From b8491d036c11fe23406f08fc1e128383e62a19e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Geckomacabre <91030858+Geckomacabre@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:03:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Series S: both upscaler choices return the title's own
 upscaler on the known build

On a Series S the title can pick AMD FidelityFX (type 7) instead of its own
upscaler (type 6). FidelityFX's output never reaches the screen here and its DLL is
refused by the host policy ("a host DLL outside the host policy: refused
amd_fidelityfx_upscaler_xbox.dll"), so the world stays black. VICTORY_UPSCALER=6
patched only the picker (+0x7e93f0); the title asks a per-frame copy of it
(+0x5400190) again every frame.

- KNOWN_BUILDS gets the master build's hash.
- With --console series-s and that build, the picker and its per-frame copy (now a
  site of its own, 32 bytes compared) return 6. VICTORY_UPSCALER=<kind> still
  overrides, now at both sites; VICTORY_TITLE_PATCHES=0 leaves the title's choice,
  =1 applies it on any console.
- Log: 'resolution: upscaler picker (the per-frame copy) (returns 6) ... Done'.

From fxceless/victory-fork #798 by KyleS98 (both sites).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
